Adaptation: Go emulation of the indexer Q/K cast. Inputs are rounded to bf16,
each group of 32 values gets one UE8M0 power-of-two scale, and values are
encoded as e2m1 codes. The scale rule is transcribed from upstream code: amax
floored at 6*2^-126, multiplied by float32(1/6), and rounded up to a power of
two through the (bits-1)>>23 exponent step, so a zero group keeps scale byte 1.
The e2m1 round-to-nearest-even tie rule with finite saturation is inferred from
the upstream cast comments; the CUDA conversion kernel itself is external to the
repository. The test composes this cast with fak's own f32 indexer score and
top-k selection to measure top-512 selection overlap against fak's bf16-widened
f32 scoring. Fak's indexer is unchanged and does not score MXFP4.

