Adaptation: Go emulation of the V4.1 KV cache casts on fak's projected rows.
Window rows, and compressed rows when the FP4 sparse KV option is off, are
rounded to bf16 and passed through fak's existing per-32 e4m3 activation
reference with a UE8M0 power-of-two scale; a boundary test shows that its
float32(1/448) multiply selects the same scale as the store kernel's division by
448. Compressed rows in the default FP4 profile are rounded to bf16 and cast per
16 values: amax floored at 6*2^-9, multiplied by float32(1/6), capped at 448,
narrowed to an e4m3 scale, inverted in float32, and the scaled values encoded as
e2m1, then dequantized to bf16, which is also what the prefill cast-back
returns. The e4m3 and e2m1 round-to-nearest-even and saturation rules are
inferred from the upstream constants and cast comments; the CUDA conversion
kernels are external to the repository. The test measures the relative L2 change
of fak's host combined attention output on a synthetic fixture.

