Adaptation: the e4m3 round trip with one UE8M0 power-of-two scale per 32 values
already existed in fak as its activation reference. The DeepInfer contribution
is the placement map: with FP8 MLP activations enabled, the bf16 FFN-norm input
to gate/up and the route-weighted SwiGLU operand to down are cast, while the
router projection and the GEMM outputs stay bf16; the norm-fused cast also
corroborates the 1e-4 amax floor and the ceil power-of-two scale rule. The
SwiGLU, route weight and down-input cast are one fused upstream kernel, so the
oracle casts the float32 weighted value directly; whether a bf16 rounding sits
before that cast is not observable upstream. The test measures expert-output
relative L2 change against fak's host bf16 expert graph on a synthetic fixture.

Float32 rotary table (internal/model/v41_rope_f32_test.go)

Upstream paths:
  deepinfer/model_executor/layers/rotary_embedding.py:35-41,68-82,109-144,195-207
