The rotary_embedding.py source derives from vLLM and HuggingFace Transformers;
its copyright lines, reproduced above, are retained as Apache-2.0 section 4(c)
requires.

Adaptation: Go float32 emulation of the V4.1 rotary table. The inverse
frequencies are built as float32 pow and reciprocal; on compressed layers the
YaRN blend follows the upstream operand order (interpolation weighted by one
minus the mask, extrapolation by the mask) with every step rounded to float32;
the angle is the float32 product of position and frequency, and cos and sin have
unit amplitude because the V4.1 config disables YaRN mscale. Layer regime,
theta and YaRN parameters come from fak's existing V4.1 rotary policy. Host pow
and trigonometry are correctly rounded, so this makes no bitwise claim against
CUDA or torch. The test measures the angle gap between fak's float64 table and
this float32 emulation at long positions; fak's table is unchanged.

