Adaptation: a named host representation of exactly 128 indexer values, packed
E2M1 low-nibble first with four per-32 UE8M0 scales. It transcribes the fused
producer's BF16 input/product boundary, amax floor 6*2^-126, FP32 multiply by
rounded 1/6, bitwise ceiling exponent and BF16 inverse power-of-two scale.
Pages have all B*64 payload bytes followed by B*4 scale bytes, with the block
stride rounded up to 32 bytes, not interleaved 68-byte rows. Producer zero rows
have scale byte 1; absent-segment byte-zero storage is not a real encoded row.
Positive host block sizes describe this layout, not device-kernel admission.
Finite-only input/output and scale-zero refusal are Fak host validation policy,
not claims about upstream consumer behavior. Inputs and page images are owned
or copied, and malformed lengths, indices and size overflow are rejected.

Corroborating encoding evidence (not copied implementation): DeepInfer pins
TileLang 0.1.15, revision a35f8ddf45eba16c21211ec8822d56ce5363036f,
src/tl_templates/cuda/cuda_fp4.h:111-124. Its CUDA conversion uses
cudaRoundNearest and packs the even element into the low nibble. CUDA FP4
documentation specifies same-sign maximum-normal saturation. Host E2M1
conversion models those rules; generated CUDA, extreme/subnormal device
behavior and end-to-end score parity have not been executed or established.
This boundary does not modify the original test-only oracle, wire live Q/K
casts or scoring, add generic dtypes/GGUF handling, or bind a device ABI. In
particular, upstream paired BF16 FMA scoring is distinct from Fak F32 scoring.
The focused host test contains source-derived literal row/page bytes, not
captured CUDA outputs.
